 rust people. When we are in a space of safety\, we are able to relax\, fee
 l comfort\, and be vulnerable.\n\n**Our Agreements:**\n1- We ask for what 
 we want an wait for a yes before touching others.\n2- We say no if we don
 ’t want to do something.\n3- We try to receive a no with grace and not t
 ake it personally.\n4- We arrive on time\, clean (as scent free as possibl
 e)\, and sober.\n5- We keep our pants/shorts on at this event. (Tops are o
 ptional\; this is a sensual space\, not a sexual space.)\n6- We are here t
 o connect with others. Connection can be verbal\, platonic\, or spicy!\n7-
  We welcome diversity. Isms and Phobias are not welcome here!\n\n**Who sho
 uld attend:**\nPeople who are interested in safely exploring touch and sen
 suality with strangers. This includes people who are single\, people who a
 re not single\, couples\, folks who are new to town and looking for connec
 tion\, people of all/any genders and sexual orientations\, people of all a
 ges (18 and up). People who understand and respect consent\, who will take
  care of themselves and people around them. This event is queer-normative.
  The guest list will include all genders\, orientations\, ages\, and perso
 nalities. If that’s not your thing… This is not the event for you.\n**
 *Who should NOT attend:***\n-People who are only looking for a sex party.\
 n-People who do not understand and respect consent.\n-People who have extr
 eme fear of setting and speaking their personal boundaries\; in order to c
 reate a safe space we need to know that you will say “no” if you feel 
 a no.\n-People who are homophobic\, racist\, sexist\, ageist\, ableist…\
 n-People under 18 years of age.\n***Schedule of the Evening***\n\n\\*6:50p
 m Doors Open\, Mix & Mingle\n\n* 7:00pm We gather in a circle to meet each
  other\, build a container\, cover consent and boundary setting and discus
 s event agreements. Then we will play a few intimacy building games to mee
 t and connect with other people in the room. Please make sure you arrive o
 n-time!\n\\*8:15pm Once the container is built we will have self directed 
 snuggling and sensual interactions until the end of the party.\n* 10:50pm 
 Closing Circle\; a time to re-center and connect as a group to verbally sh
 are anything that came up at the event or to voice gratitude to someone(s)
  you enjoyed interacting with.\n\\*11:00pm cleanup & head home\; you are w
 elcome to help.\n\n**We take individual and group safety seriously!** If y
 ou experience\, see\, or know that one of our participants is not safe to 
 be at this event we want to know about it. We are committed to doing our b
 est to create a safe environment which means that if someone is causing ha
 rm (physical or mental) that person is not welcome here (this includes har
 m that takes place outside of our events). We stand behind survivors and k
 now that some of our participants are here to heal from touch based trauma
 .\n\nThese events are not "gender balanced"[. Check out our website for mo
 re information about this decision.](http://holdmeavl.com/why-i-dont-gende
 r-balance-events/)\n\n**Simple definitions/clarifications-** Platonic- mar
 ked by the absence of romance or sex.\nMost of the interactions we have wi
 th friends and strangers are platonic.\nSensual- gratification of the sens
 es or the indulgence of appetite.\nWe might feel sensual when we feel some
 one's breath on our neck or experience a extra long and slow caress.\nSexu
 al- having or involving sex.\nOften involving one more more peoples genita
 ls\; perhaps seeking orgasm.\n\\*Refund Policy- Full refund if you cancel 
 7 days before the event or you cancel due to illness\, emergency\, or dire
 ct exposure to covid. Credit towards a future event if you cancel more tha
 n 3 days before an event. No refund if you cancel within 2 days of the eve
 nt or no-show.
