SUMMARY:Nov 7th Morning Community Cuddles
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Cuddle Collective\nPlease note- If you want to atten
 d this event you need to purchase a ticket- We advertise in many places an
 d only paid tickets will reserve your space. **[Click HERE to reserve your
  ticket!](https://www.zeffy.com/en-US/ticketing/nov-7th-morning-community-
 cuddle)**[ ](https://www.zeffy.com/en-US/ticketing/nov-7th-morning-communi
 ty-cuddle)\n\n**This is a non-sexual touch based event that invites partic
 ipants to explore platonic intimacy in a safe environment** with like-mind
 ed people. We respect personal boundaries and through a supportive framewo
 rk of mutual agreements that maximize safety and create a space of easy op
 enness and compassionate connection.\nAt this event we have the chance to 
 normalize touch with clear boundaries\; this is a space for respectful\, c
 onsent-based touch. We allow ourselves to be seen. We have fun.\nWe welcom
 e people of all backgrounds\, genders\, ethnicities\, relationship styles\
 , sexualities\, sizes\, and ages (18+).\n\n**THE RULES**\n\n1. Clothes sta
 y on for the whole event.\n2. You do not have to touch anyone at this even
 t.\n3. You must receive a verbal YES before you touch anyone.\n4. Take car
 e of yourself and those you choose to interact with.\n5. Speak up if you h
 ave a question\, concern\, or if you need assistance with anything during 
 the event.\n6. All emotions are welcome- we love vulnerability.\n**WHY CUD
 DLE?**\nTouch is a basic human need\, and many of us do not get enough\; m
 ost people don’t even know they are missing touch\, or have a way to ask
  for touch without sexualizing it. We believe deeply in the power of touch
 \, and the importance of communication and consent in creating a safe spac
 e for touch.\nCUDDLING WITH STRANGERS\nCuddling with strangers sounds weir
 d or scary to most people. “Will I like it?” “What if someone wants 
 to touch me and I don’t want to?” “What if I say yes and it’s not 
 what I want?” “What if I really want to touch someone and they say no?
 ” These are all normal questions. The answer is that this is a space cre
 ated to ask for exactly what you want\, and receive NOTHING you don’t wa
 nt. Many people start out nervous at a cuddle event & most are really glad
  they came.\n\n**Schedule:**\n6:50-7pm: Arrive with snacks to share! Get c
 omfortable\, meet\, mingle\, & snack.\n7:05pm: Welcome Circle- its mandato
 ry. We will set our container\, talk about personal boundaries\, communica
 tion\, & consent.\n7:15pm: Icebreakers and connective activities.\n8:00pm:
  Open cuddling! You MUST ask and get a verbal ‘yes’ before touching or
  cuddling with anybody at this event. If you are not sure how to do this 
 – great! – we will talk about it during the welcome circle.\n10:50pm: 
 Closing Circle\, cleanup and head home.\n**ETIQUETTE**\n\n\\*ARRIVE ON TIM
 E: It is important that all participants arrive before the Welcome Circle.
  The Welcome Circle serves the purpose of creating the safe space for cons
 ensual\, non-sexual touch between participants and making sure that everyo
 ne is informed about consent.\n\n* Please arrive clean & as scent free as 
 possible.\n\\*BE SOBER: Please do not drink or smoke before or at this eve
 nt.\n\n**WHAT TO BRING:** personal water bottle and snacks to share\, a fr
 iend\, a date – whatever cuddle accessories you like! The only thing tha
 t you are required to bring is a clean and sober you.\n\nThese events are 
 not "gender balanced".\n\n**We take individual and group safety seriously!
 ** If you experience\, see\, or know that one of our participants is not s
 afe to be at this event we want to know about it. We are committed to doin
 g our best to create a safe environment which means that if someone is cau
 sing harm (physical or mental) that person is not welcome here (this inclu
 des harm that takes place outside of our events). We stand behind survivor
 s and know that some of our participants are here to heal from touch based
  trauma.\n\n\\*refund policy-\nFull refund if you cancel 7 days before the
  event or you cancel due to illness\, emergency\, or direct exposure to co
 vid/flu.\nCredit towards a future event if you cancel more than 3 days bef
 ore an event.\nNo refund if you cancel within 2 days of the event or no-sh
 ow.
